From: Uke Linux project <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cpufreq: qcom-hw: retain the Uke OEM boost permission

Uke and the same-SoC OnePlus OSS driver enable CPUFreq boost by default.
Restore that permission for the exact Uke/SM7675 machine before policies
are registered. Keep other machines unchanged and leave runtime control
with the standard CPUFreq boost interface.

This does not add frequencies, voltages or minimum-frequency requests.
Only firmware LUT rows already admitted by the existing EPSS parser are
available. A domain without reduced-core boost rows gains no extra OPP.

Sources (GPL-2.0-only):
MiCode/Xiaomi_Kernel_OpenSource 5712080a4b0c0b1a879e6d145c601c649ddaddfd
OnePlusOSS/android_kernel_oneplus_sm7675 fc892483f1d61f245924681eb5abd563564d9cba
drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-hw.c, cpufreq_qcom_hw_driver.boost_enabled

--- a/drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-hw.c
+++ b/drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-hw.c
@@ -990,1 +990,6 @@ static int qcom_cpufreq_hw_driver_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
+	/* Preserve the OEM permission without changing the fused EPSS table. */
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("xiaomi,uke") &&
+	    of_machine_is_compatible("qcom,sm7675"))
+		cpufreq_qcom_hw_driver.boost_enabled = true;
+
 	ret = cpufreq_register_driver(&cpufreq_qcom_hw_driver);
